experiment: ctxvocab
  instrument        ctxvocab   trial seed 000000000135e703   2428 trials
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  the question      ctxgrid names FOUR words on two axes at +0.137.
                    aimaxes put ~2.6 levels on each axis, predicting a
                    capacity near 2.6 x 2.6 = 6.7 -- a PRODUCT. Does the
                    excess survive six words, and nine?
  the design        the SPAN is fixed and the spacing HALVES against the
                    k=4 anchor: more words inside the same learned reach.
                    So a falling excess is what resolution ALONE predicts,
                    and the headline cannot be a capacity curve. THREE arms
                    instead: k6, k9, and k9+ (the same nine words with 1.5x
                    the ticks, matching k=6's TRIALS PER WORD). F1 demands
                    59 Hz in all three, so delivered F1 spacing separates
                    teaching budget from word interference.
  the spacing       F1 59 Hz and F2 150 Hz adjacent at k=6 and k=9,
                    against 118 / 300 at ctxgrid's k=4: HALF.
  the null          each k brings its OWN no-index arm. `nearest` has no
                    fixed chance level and the geometry changes with k.

