  WHAT DAMAGES THE DELIVERY  (F1 demand is 59 Hz in all three arms)
    k6   delivered   18.0 +/-  2.8 Hz
    k9   delivered    6.0 +/-  2.9 Hz
    k9+  delivered    6.2 +/-  2.1 Hz   (same nine words, 1.5x ticks)
    BUDGET      k9+ - k9    +0.1 +/-  3.5 Hz (0.0 SE)  <- teaching per word
    VOCABULARY  k9+ - k6   -11.8 +/-  3.5 Hz (3.4 SE)  <- nine words vs six,
                                                      trials/word MATCHED
    levels the F1 reach holds at k9+:  span 12.4 Hz / 2 x scatter 44.0  ->  1.1 levels

  THE SCORE IS GEOMETRY. At every k the creature's per-axis accuracy is
  within 2 SE of what its own DELIVERED spacing and scatter predict, so
  the falling excess is not a readout failure and `nearest` is behaving.
  The question is what shrinks the DELIVERY, and F1 answers it cleanly
  because its demand is 59 Hz in all three arms.

  VOCABULARY COSTS REACH. With trials per word MATCHED, nine words
  deliver -11.8 +/- 3.5 Hz of F1 separation against six (3.4 SE,
  clearing the 3 SE bar). The words INTERFERE: each one added costs
  the others reach, and at k=9 the delivered span holds ~1.1
  distinguishable levels. A capacity limit proper -- on the REACH the
  bias can build, where ctxscale's ~118 Hz asymptote and
  ceiling-is-an-exponent already put the ceiling.
  The teaching budget is NOT excluded: k9+ - k9 is +0.1 +/- 3.5 Hz
  (0.0 SE, n=18), which at the 3 SE bar still admits up to 10.8 Hz --
  91% of the vocabulary term. More teaching is a SMALLER effect than
  more words, and that is the whole of what this arm shows.
